  "result": "Full test suite passes (1419 passed, no failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was in `src/click/testing.py`'s `BytesIOCopy` class, used by `CliRunner` to back `sys.stdout`/`sys.stderr` during `invoke()`. It was a plain `io.BytesIO`, which doesn't have a real file descriptor \u2014 calling `.fileno()` on it (as `subprocess.run` does when given a file-like `stdout=`/`stderr=` argument) always raises `io.UnsupportedOperation`.\n\nFix: `BytesIOCopy` now lazily creates a real, file-descriptor-backed `tempfile.TemporaryFile()` the first time `fileno()` is called, and returns that descriptor. Regular buffered `write()` calls still go to both the in-memory `BytesIO` and the mirrored `copy_to` stream as before, while `getvalue()` now also incorporates any bytes written directly to the fd-backed temp file (e.g. by a subprocess), preserving existing capture behavior for the common (non-fd) case and fixing the crash for the fd case.",
